      "name": "flushable-containers",
      "title": "Flushable containers",
      "description": "A flushable container is a named store that accumulates by design — a trash you can recover from, a review preview, a console log. It declares a buffer limit, badges when over it, and offers three flush actions: flush all, trim to limit, and select to prune. What \"flush\" means, and which end of the order is expendable, are declared per container and differ.",
